  "store_10_to_20m": "ACOLITE (acolite/sentinel2/l1_convert.py, read_band) warps each band to the 20 m grid with gdal.Warp(resampleAlg='average') and GDAL's default overviewLevel AUTO, so for the 10 m bands B02 B03 B04 B08 it reads the JPEG 2000 file's own 20 m resolution level (the wavelet low-pass), NOT the 2x2 mean. Measured on S2B_16PCC_20180611 B08 (full tile): ACOLITE's read_band output equals JP2 overview 0 exactly (median |diff to 2x2 mean| 20 DN, max 5868; to the NW sub-pixel 9 DN); gdal.Warp with overviewLevel='NONE' gives the 2x2 mean to 0.5 DN (uint16 rounding). Fitted kernel of the store's rho_b08 on the 10 m DN (59,377 cells, R2 0.992): 0.635 on the NW sub-pixel, 0.21/0.17/0.13/0.07 on its E/S/W/N neighbours, negative lobes; centre of mass ~7 m north-west of the cell centre. B06/B11 are native 20 m and untouched (Spearman store vs MARIDA = 1.000)."
 },
